WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:09.700
Section three-fourteen point six provides a limited exception for financial institutions maintaining customer information concerning fewer than five thousand consumers.

2
00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:24.680
The exception applies only to the detailed written risk-assessment elements in paragraph b one, the specified periodic testing provisions in paragraph d two, the written incident-response-plan requirement in paragraph h, and the governing-body reporting requirement in paragraph i.

3
00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:28.140
It is not a general exemption from the Safeguards Rule.

4
00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:37.300
An institution relying on this provision should document how it counts consumers, which customer information is included, the measurement date, and who approved the conclusion.

5
00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:43.560
Remaining obligations still require a risk-based information security program and applicable safeguards.

6
00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:57.740
Voluntarily using a written assessment, incident plan, testing schedule, or governance report may be prudent, but the organization should distinguish voluntary control design from a claim about what the exception legally requires.

7
00:00:58.020 --> 00:01:04.420
Implementation becomes manageable when regulatory clauses are mapped to owners, procedures, systems, and evidence.

8
00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:07.960
Governance evidence includes designation and oversight records.

9
00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:13.980
Risk evidence includes scope, criteria, treatment decisions, and reassessment.

10
00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:24.480
Control evidence includes configurations, approvals, reviews, logs, testing, training, provider assessments, incident records, and remediation.

11
00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:30.980
A document created immediately before an audit is weak evidence of a control that was supposed to operate throughout the year.

12
00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:38.460
Prioritize gaps according to customer-information exposure, likelihood, consequence, and dependencies.

13
00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:48.720
Manage exceptions with a defined scope, rationale, approving authority, compensating controls, residual risk, expiration, and review trigger.

14
00:01:48.820 --> 00:01:57.780
A roadmap should identify accountable owners, prerequisites, milestones, validation methods, and the evidence expected when work is complete.

15
00:01:58.060 --> 00:02:05.660
Internal compliance review, legal analysis, technical testing, and independent assurance answer different questions.

16
00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:12.080
Governing bodies and senior officers need decision-useful reporting rather than raw control inventories.

17
00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:23.460
The Qualified Individual should be able to explain current risk, significant control decisions, provider exposure, test results, events, remediation, and recommended changes.

18
00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:33.800
Treat implementation as a continuing management cycle: establish scope, assess risk, operate safeguards, test results, correct weaknesses, and update the program.
